WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:01.453
Tree rings.

00:00:01.908 --> 00:00:04.586
Width, density, isotopes.

00:00:05.039 --> 00:00:07.625
Conditions experienced by trees.

00:00:08.079 --> 00:00:09.454
Ice cores.

00:00:09.908 --> 00:00:12.836
Isotopes, dust, gas bubbles.

00:00:13.289 --> 00:00:15.836
Climate and atmospheric records.

00:00:16.289 --> 00:00:17.954
Lake sediments.

00:00:18.408 --> 00:00:20.947
Pollen, chemistry, varves.

00:00:21.408 --> 00:00:26.171
Different archives record environmental conditions through different processes.

00:00:26.632 --> 00:00:31.992
Compare what each measures and the time interval represented by an observation.

00:00:32.795 --> 00:00:34.921
Compare with observations.

00:00:35.376 --> 00:00:38.810
Establish which conditions the proxy responds to.

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:41.699
Consider multiple influences.

00:00:42.153 --> 00:00:46.238
Ring width can reflect age and competition as well as climate.

00:00:46.692 --> 00:00:48.883
Check the range of application.

00:00:49.337 --> 00:00:54.343
Relationships can vary with region, season, species and timescale.

00:00:54.797 --> 00:00:59.363
Separate the measured quantity from the environmental interpretation and test their

00:00:59.376 --> 00:01:04.252
relationship using observations or other independent evidence.

00:01:05.055 --> 00:01:10.418
A record may resolve individual years while its calendar position remains uncertain.

00:01:10.873 --> 00:01:15.327
Closely spaced measurements do not guarantee equally precise ages.

00:01:15.781 --> 00:01:21.512
Read temporal resolution and dating uncertainty as separate properties of a record.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.283
Align the timescales.

00:01:24.738 --> 00:01:28.876
Check years, seasons, calibration and reference years.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.350
Compare the same variable.

00:01:31.804 --> 00:01:35.712
Early-spring temperature differs from summer moisture conditions.

00:01:36.173 --> 00:01:38.330
Investigate mismatches.

00:01:38.791 --> 00:01:44.173
Consider uncertainty, response lag, regional variation and preservation.

00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:48.416
Check whether records represent the same area and season.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:54.708
Apparent disagreements can arise because they describe different environmental targets.
